					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tMbiSEs3hhmotVQmx",
					"name": "Necrodermis (Warrior)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 50, all locations. Weak Points 4 (per framework.md): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 4 or less means it found a joint or seam and DR is halved (25) against that hit. Eye- slit optics run at DR 25 (half the body DR) rather than 50 -- treat a called or random shot to the eye as hitting DR 25.\n\nLore: Necrodermis is a Necron's body and its armour at once: a skin of near-indestructible living metal with no separate suit to strip away. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Necron fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that necrodermis is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Necron anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Necrons"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 50,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 50
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TQFjbpGcNuz-0MIF3",
			"name": "Body Lens: Immortal",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Immortals are a Necron dynasty's elite guard: built to a sturdier, more expensive pattern than a Warrior and trusted with real tactical initiative rather than pure rote obedience. Consistently described across Codex background as a step up from Warriors in every respect.\n\nDesign: 226 (Attribute Modifiers) + 400 (Necrodermis DR 80, 5/level) = 626 points, added to Necron Physiology's 224 for 850 points of physiology and body alone. See the Necron Immortal template.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
